1
00:00:00,256 --> 00:00:03,669
Jobs and Queue is the primary view while durable work runs.

2
00:00:03,968 --> 00:00:09,344
Filter the status, expand the record and read timestamps, diagnostics, logs

3
00:00:09,429 --> 00:00:10,851
and the linked configuration.

4
00:00:11,122 --> 00:00:15,111
A verification failure can matter even when the subprocess returned zero.

5
00:00:15,474 --> 00:00:18,162
Preserve terminal evidence before retention cleanup.

6
00:00:18,418 --> 00:00:21,439
Removing a queue record does not undo a target operation.

7
00:00:21,936 --> 00:00:26,544
Open Approvals and inspect the request, exact input, target and requester

8
00:00:26,586 --> 00:00:27,056
notes.

9
00:00:27,354 --> 00:00:30,547
Follow the required reviewer separation and expiry rules.

10
00:00:30,880 --> 00:00:34,720
Approve only the intended change; a deployment approval does not

11
00:00:34,848 --> 00:00:37,003
automatically approve later configuration.

12
00:00:37,323 --> 00:00:40,642
If the configuration changes, obtain its matching approval.

13
00:00:40,975 --> 00:00:45,327
Historical approval records support audit, but do not establish that the

14
00:00:45,369 --> 00:00:47,415
requested operation ran successfully.

15
00:00:47,838 --> 00:00:51,678
Choose a repeatable action with a supported scheduled path, supply its

16
00:00:51,721 --> 00:00:55,817
reviewed input and enter the five-field U T C cron expression.

17
00:00:56,158 --> 00:01:00,062
Test manually, then enable and verify an actual scheduled run.

18
00:01:00,340 --> 00:01:01,542
Pause for maintenance.

19
00:01:01,892 --> 00:01:05,987
Mandatory-approval workflows may be rejected by automation surfaces without

20
00:01:06,201 --> 00:01:08,014
an appropriate approval binding.

21
00:01:08,334 --> 00:01:11,427
Do not assume missed runs are replayed after downtime.

22
00:01:11,811 --> 00:01:15,651
Parallel Exec submits the same supported legacy workflow for multiple

23
00:01:15,950 --> 00:01:17,337
labelled site inputs.

24
00:01:17,657 --> 00:01:22,308
Check isolation of targets, credentials, addresses, images and services

25
00:01:22,564 --> 00:01:23,172
first.

26
00:01:23,524 --> 00:01:27,364
This screen is not proof that classic Foundation V M can run overlapping

27
00:01:27,449 --> 00:01:28,196
sessions.

28
00:01:28,558 --> 00:01:32,797
Use separately supported deployment paths and coordinate resource ownership.

29
00:01:33,068 --> 00:01:36,908
Inspect every site result because an aggregate success indicator can hide

30
00:01:37,036 --> 00:01:38,046
partial outcomes.

31
00:01:38,529 --> 00:01:42,284
A cancellation request or process interruption does not guarantee that an

32
00:01:42,327 --> 00:01:44,002
external operation stopped.

33
00:01:44,312 --> 00:01:48,024
Inspect Foundation or Prism and reconcile actual state.

34
00:01:48,365 --> 00:01:50,925
Keep successful steps and uncertainty recorded.

35
00:01:51,224 --> 00:01:55,350
For recovery, use its reconciliation and next-step linking controls.

36
00:01:55,679 --> 00:02:00,159
Never repeat destructive imaging or an uncertain password change simply to

37
00:02:00,202 --> 00:02:02,541
produce a cleaner execution history.
